msgid " (NOT \"90 minutes\"). The system recognizes \"min\" as the suffix for minute-based calculations."
msgstr ""

#: build-admin/300.js:1
msgid "Either the twilight angle (in degrees) or minutes after sunset for Maghrib prayer."
msgstr ""

#: build-admin/300.js:1
msgid " 4°, 4.5°, or "
msgstr ""

#: build-admin/300.js:1
msgid "Minutes to add after solar midday (zenith) to ensure Dhuhr begins after the sun has truly passed its highest point."
msgstr ""

#: build-admin/300.js:1
msgid "How many times the engine re-runs the whole prayer-time computation. Each pass uses the previous pass's times as the starting point, which refines the position of the sun used for the angles. It is a "
msgstr ""

#: build-admin/300.js:1
msgid "precision"
msgstr ""

#: build-admin/300.js:1
msgid " setting — it never changes which method or convention is used, only how accurately the same times are calculated."
msgstr ""

#: build-admin/300.js:1
msgid "Why it matters:"
msgstr ""

#: build-admin/300.js:1
msgid " the library starts from approximate seeds (Fajr 05:00, Dhuhr 12:00, …) and the sun's declination depends on the time of day, so a couple of passes let each prayer converge on its true value. The difference between 2 and 5 passes is a matter of seconds."
msgstr ""

#: build-admin/300.js:1
msgid " for normal use. Only raise it (up to 5) at very high latitudes (e.g. northern UK, Scandinavia) where convergence is slower. The panel clamps the value between 1 and 5."
msgstr ""

